Input: {"question": "Which educational institution did Willy Schwabacher attend?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 163, "text": "As Willy Schwabacher delved deeper into the world of numismatics, his fascination with the intricacies of coin design and the stories they told only grew stronger."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 164, "end": 367, "text": "It was during his undergraduate years at the University of Nottingham, surrounded by the historic architecture and vibrant cultural scene of the East Midlands, that his passion truly began to take shape."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 368, "end": 544, "text": "Willy would often spend hours pouring over dusty tomes in the university's sprawling library, uncovering hidden gems and obscure references that shed new light on his research."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 545, "end": 713, "text": "His favorite haunt was the George Green Library, where the musty scent of old books and the soft hum of fluorescent lights created the perfect atmosphere for immersion."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 714, "end": 872, "text": "It was there, nestled between shelves stacked high with volumes on art history and archaeology, that he stumbled upon an obscure treatise on medieval coinage."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 873, "end": 917, "text": "The author, a little-known scholar named Dr."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 918, "end": 1078, "text": "Emilia Fothergill, had a way of bringing the past to life with her vivid descriptions of 12th-century minting techniques and the rivalries between royal courts."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1079, "end": 1211, "text": "Willy was captivated by her writing style, which seemed to dance across the page like the intricate patterns on a Byzantine solidus."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1212, "end": 1325, "text": "He devoured the entire book in a single sitting, his mind racing with the possibilities of how he could apply Dr."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1326, "end": 1368, "text": "Fothergill's theories to his own research."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1369, "end": 1453, "text": "As the semester drew to a close, Willy decided to take a chance and reach out to Dr."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1454, "end": 1559, "text": "Fothergill, hoping to discuss her work and perhaps even secure an introduction to the academic community."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1560, "end": 1767, "text": "To his surprise, she responded promptly, inviting him to meet at the university's Department of Archaeology, where she was scheduled to deliver a guest lecture on the numismatic significance of the Crusades."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1768, "end": 1875, "text": "The day of the lecture arrived, and Willy made his way to the department, his heart racing with excitement."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1876, "end": 1930, "text": "As he entered the crowded seminar room, he spotted Dr."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1931, "end": 2027, "text": "Fothergill, a statuesque woman with silver hair and piercing green eyes, standing at the podium."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2028, "end": 2174, "text": "Her words were like a symphony, weaving together threads of history, politics, and art to create a rich tapestry that left the audience entranced."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2175, "end": 2236, "text": "After the lecture, Willy mustered the courage to approach Dr."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2237, "end": 2338, "text": "Fothergill, introducing himself and sharing his own research on the coinage of the Holy Roman Empire."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2339, "end": 2490, "text": "To his delight, she was impressed by his knowledge and enthusiasm, offering words of encouragement and a valuable connection to the academic community."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 121, "text": "Title: The Numismatist's Academic Pursuits: Unveiling Willy Schwabacher's Connection to Technical University of Darmstadt"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 123, "end": 280, "text": "In the realm of numismatics, few names shine as brightly as Willy Schwabacher, a German numismatist whose contributions to the field are still revered today."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 281, "end": 402, "text": "While his expertise in coins and medals is well-documented, a lesser-known aspect of his life is his academic background."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 403, "end": 632, "text": "A crucial piece of evidence reveals that Schwabacher attended the prestigious Technical University of Darmstadt, a German institution renowned for its excellence in science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM) fields."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 633, "end": 776, "text": "This narrative delves into the life of Willy Schwabacher, exploring the context and significance of his connection to this esteemed university."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 777, "end": 900, "text": "Born in the late 19th century, Willy Schwabacher grew up in a Germany undergoing rapid industrialization and modernization."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 901, "end": 1016, "text": "As a young man, he developed a fascination with coins and medals, which would eventually become his life's passion."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1017, "end": 1131, "text": "However, before devoting himself fully to numismatics, Schwabacher recognized the importance of a solid education."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1132, "end": 1350, "text": "In the early 20th century, he made the decision to enroll at the Technical University of Darmstadt, an institution that had been at the forefront of scientific and technological advancements since its founding in 1877."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1351, "end": 1563, "text": "Founded during the reign of Grand Duke Ludwig IV of Hesse, the Technical University of Darmstadt was established to provide education and training in the fields of engineering, architecture, and natural sciences."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1564, "end": 1712, "text": "By the time Schwabacher attended, the university had already gained a reputation for excellence, attracting students from across Germany and beyond."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1713, "end": 1950, "text": "The university's strong emphasis on practical application and innovative research created an environment that fostered intellectual curiosity and creativity – qualities that would serve Schwabacher well in his future numismatic pursuits."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1951, "end": 2109, "text": "Schwabacher's time at the Technical University of Darmstadt was marked by intense academic rigor and a deepening of his understanding of the natural sciences."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2110, "end": 2335, "text": "His coursework in subjects like chemistry, physics, and mathematics provided a solid foundation for his later work in numismatics, where an understanding of metallurgy, materials science, and historical context was essential."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2336, "end": 2531, "text": "The university's emphasis on experimentation and hands-on learning also instilled in Schwabacher a meticulous attention to detail, a trait that would become a hallmark of his numismatic research."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "University of Nottingham", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "Technical University of Darmstadt", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Willy Schwabacher", "scope": "undergraduate years", "claim": "Willy Schwabacher attended the University of Nottingham during his undergraduate years.", "answer": "University of Nottingham", "quote": "It was during his undergraduate years at the University of Nottingham, surrounded by the historic architecture and vibrant cultural scene of the East Midlands, that his passion truly began to take shape.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Willy Schwabacher", "scope": "education", "claim": "Willy Schwabacher attended the Technical University of Darmstadt.", "answer": "Technical University of Darmstadt", "quote": "A crucial piece of evidence reveals that Schwabacher attended the prestigious Technical University of Darmstadt, a German institution renowned for its excellence in science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM) fields. This narrative delves into the life of Willy Schwabacher, exploring the context and significance of his connection to this esteemed university. Born in the late 19th century, Willy Schwabacher grew up in a Germany undergoing rapid industrialization and modernization. As a young man, he developed a fascination with coins and medals, which would eventually become his life's passion. However, before devoting himself fully to numismatics, Schwabacher recognized the importance of a solid education. In the early 20th century, he made the decision to enroll at the Technical University of Darmstadt, an institution that had been at the forefront of scientific and technological advancements since its founding in 1877.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["University of Nottingham", "Technical University of Darmstadt"]}
